__d(function(g,r,i,a,m,e,d){Object.defineProperty(e,"__esModule",{value:!0}),e.LEGAL=void 0;e.LEGAL={privacy:{key:"privacy",title:"Privacy",updated:"3 September 2026",body:["SayHeloo keeps the places you save, the trips and parties you plan, and the few settings you choose. This page says what that means in plain words.","## What we keep","The links you share and the places they turn into (name, city, coordinates, the photo and rating Google returns for that place). Your trips, their dates and what you marked as booked. Your parties, their stops, invites and the messages in a party's chat. Your Traveler profile and posts, if you become one. Your name, home airport, phone and currency, if you set them. Your photos and videos in a place's Memories. What Heloo remembers: a handful of preferences you stated, which you can erase one by one on the You tab.","## Where it lives","On your phone first. When you sign in with an email code, the same things are kept on our servers (run on Supabase) so they follow you to any device. A guest's saves live only on that device.","## What we don't do","We don't sell your data. We don't show ads. We don't read your TikTok, Instagram or X accounts; we only look at the single link you hand us. We don't post anywhere on your behalf. We don't know where you are unless you allow it for a near-me question or the map, and we don't store your location. We don't move money: bookings happen on the partner's site, and a party's split is only calculated.","## Who else sees data","Google, to name a place from a link and to draw the map; Google's own privacy terms apply to that lookup. Anthropic, which runs the model behind Heloo; it receives your question and the places you asked about, not your account. Booking partners (Booking.com, GetYourGuide, Google Flights and others) only when you open their site from a booking card. A trip's group and a party's guests see what you share with them by link.","## Your choices","Delete any place, trip, party or post yourself. Erase what Heloo remembers, line by line. Delete your whole account from the You tab; it removes everything above, for good, within minutes.","## Contact","support@sayheloo.com"]},terms:{key:"terms",title:"Terms",updated:"3 September 2026",body:["SayHeloo is a tool for finding, saving and planning around real places. Using it means agreeing to the few rules below.","## The app is honest, and so are you","Save places you actually want, post takes you actually hold. Travelers post real places with a real take; ads dressed as tips, invented places or content you have no right to share get a post removed and can end a Traveler's status.","## What SayHeloo is not","It is not a booking agent, a travel agency or a bank. A booking card opens a partner's website; the reservation, its price and its terms are between you and that partner. Heloo is a companion, not a guarantee: it never claims a table or a room is free. A party's split is a calculation to help friends settle up; no money moves through SayHeloo.","## Accounts","Anyone can save as a guest. Signing in with an email code lets your world follow you, and lets you plan trips with friends and open group hubs. Booking needs a profile with your name. You are responsible for what happens under your sign-in.","## Content and rights","The links, captions, photos and videos you add stay yours. You give SayHeloo the right to keep and show them to you, and to the people you share them with, so the app can work. Traveler posts are public by nature. Videos from TikTok, Instagram, YouTube and X are never copied or rehosted; the app keeps the link and shows what the platform allows.","## Availability","SayHeloo is early. Features change, chapters arrive, and the service can pause. We keep the record of what changed in the app's own version notes.","## Ending","You can delete your account at any time from the You tab. We can close accounts that break the rules above.","## Contact","support@sayheloo.com"]},attribution:{key:"attribution",title:"Data & attribution",updated:"3 September 2026",body:["SayHeloo stands on other people's data and says so.","## Places and the map","Place names, photos, ratings, addresses and opening hours come from Google Places, and the map is Google Maps. Their content is theirs; the app shows it as it comes and refreshes it rather than keeping copies. Where place data appears without a Google map, it carries the Google Maps mark.","## Videos","TikTok, Instagram, YouTube and X videos belong to the people who made them. SayHeloo keeps the link and opens the original; it never copies a video.","## Weather","When Heloo mentions the weather, the forecast comes from Open-Meteo (open data, CC BY 4.0).","## Heloo","Heloo's answers are generated by Claude, a model made by Anthropic, working only from your saves, Travelers' takes and labelled outside picks.","## Booking partners","Booking cards open Booking.com, GetYourGuide, Google Flights, Uber and Google Maps. SayHeloo may earn a commission from some of these when you book; it never changes what you pay.","## Software","Built with Expo and React Native, Supabase, the Google Maps JavaScript API, and open-source libraries under their own licenses."]},help:{key:"help",title:"Help & contact",updated:"3 September 2026",body:["Write to support@sayheloo.com. A person reads it.","## Saving from a video","Share the video to SayHeloo from the video's Share menu. If SayHeloo isn't in that list on your phone yet, copy the link, open the Wishlist and paste it into the gold plus. Or type the place's name. If the platform hides the details, the card asks for the caption; paste it and the place is found.","## Something looks wrong","Tell us which screen and what you expected; a screenshot helps. Say which version you're on: it's printed at the bottom of the You tab.","## Deleting things","Any save, trip, party or post can be deleted where it lives. Your whole account can be deleted from the You tab."]}}},880,[]);
